Republicans senator Cory Gardner of  Colorado says the president made the  right decision he's chairman of the  Foreign Relations Subcommittee on East  Asia the Pacific and international  cybersecurity policy senator Gardner is  with us from Denver good morning senator  let's start with why this deal fell  apart you say it was the right thing for  the president to do why was it the right  thing for the president to do well I  think we've known all along that if  there was any sense that Kim jong-un was  not committed to denuclearization this  meeting wouldn't occur and in the weeks  leading up to the summit meetings were  canceled that we had the State  Department officials meeting in  Singapore with North Korean officials  those meetings were canceled phone calls  were not returned they canceled meetings  with the South Koreans and so I I think  it's appropriate to make sure that when  we get to this summit it's not about  games it's not about propaganda  it's about denuclearization isn't this  why these summits though are worked out  beforehand at a lower level so that you  don't have national prestige at stake  between the leaders this early in the  negotiating process because obviously  North Korea is not going to say yeah  we'll give up the entire program right  off the bat well I think what's happened  is that that those planning efforts were  being made if you look at the meeting  that was going to be held in Singapore  that was all leading up to the summit in  Singapore and so phone calls that  weren't returned they were going to be  planning efforts for Singapore I think  what happened over the past couple of  weeks kim jeong-hoon either has started  to lack the support within his closest  confidants the old guard perhaps putting  pressure on him as saying this isn't the  way your father did things you can't do  this or maybe even the meeting with  President Xi as has been talked about  publicly had changed the results a  little bit of Kim Jong Un's attitude as  it related to the summit did China try  to bring him in a little closer and  saying hey we're nervous about making a  deal with the Americans and so we'll  relax the sanctions those are all  questions that we have to have answers  for that we have to continue our maximum  pressure doctrine but I hope that we can  get back to a position where we do  indeed have a deal on denuclearization  sooner I want to talk about just how  damaging this may be to the u.s.  position as you referred to there was a  White House deputy chief of staff  waiting in Singapore for North Korean  officials and was stood up by the North  Koreans  but now the North Koreans have gotten  public recognition they may get an  easing of sanctions they can continue  with their nuclear program  doesn't this just strengthen China in  the end well to be clear there we know  easing of sanctions in fact the  commitment that I received yesterday  from the Secretary of State I was at the  White House meeting with national  security adviser at Bolton  we will double down on our sanctions in  fact Congress is prepared to pass  additional sanctions legislation that  I've put in place called the lead act  it's already out of the Foreign  Relations Committee just needs to move  through the full Senate now in the house  we can double down on these sanctions to  further isolate North Korea economically  and diplomatically to continue to  ratchet up our pressure but I don't  think this is any kind of a win for  North Korea in fact this fits a pattern  of misbehavior his promises by his  family have been broken over the decades  many times and so this isn't anything  new what we see is an internal challenge  and struggle between kim jeong-hoon a  challenge between this peacemaker to  bring his Hermit Kingdom out of the  darkness and this challenge the struggle  between the propagandist a pattern of  behavior by North Korea that gets global  attention and then they break the  promise and in this instance it looks  like the propagandist won over in that  internal debate all right senator  Gardner thank you so much for joining us  we appreciate it
 

